<worksheet >
    <title>DC-5 Lagrange Multipliers</title>
  <introduction>
    <p> To earn an M on this outcome, you will need to give the correct system, 
      give the correct critical points and classifications; to earn a P on this outcome, 
      you will need to give the correct system and give the correct critical points.</p>
  </introduction>  
  <page>
    <exercise>
        <p>Given <m>f(x,y,z)=3x+y+2z</m> on the ellipsoid <m>3x^2+y^2+2z^2=24</m>, use the method of 
          Lagrange multipliers to find the extreme values of the function.</p>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>